All verified against the code. Here's the review of PR #2 (`feat/web-demo`).

**Verdict:** No crash-class or security bugs; the wire seams and engine call sites are consistent and the branch builds/tests clean. But the line-by-line and cross-file passes turned up several real correctness/UX defects that survived the earlier review (they live in code paths the first pass didn't exercise), plus a couple of concrete cleanups. Ranked, most severe first:

```json
[
  {
    "file": "internal/server/static/js/views/dashboard.js",
    "line": 203,
    "summary": "Latency line is gated on this-second success count (v.ok > 0) instead of the rolling window, so any zero-completion second blanks the chart despite the collector's 10s rolling percentiles; history.js:94 has the same bug on stored-run replay.",
    "failure_scenario": "Under high concurrency / a slow forge, a bucket can have v.ok===0 while the 10s window still holds samples (v.p95_ms non-zero). The client pushes null, so charts.lat gets a gap and the latency line flickers/breaks exactly during the slow moments the rolling window exists to keep visible. Gate on v.p95_ms > 0 (rolling data present), not per-second ok."
  },
  {
    "file": "internal/server/static/js/views/newrun.js",
    "line": 232,
    "summary": "submit() computes allDemo over ALL target rows (blanks included, isDemo('')=false) while updateGate() computes it over remote-filtered rows, so the two disagree when a demo target coexists with a blank target card.",
    "failure_scenario": "Custom mode: a demo:// target plus a leftover blank row. updateGate sees allDemo=true, hides the confirm checkbox and enables Start. submit sees allDemo=false, so confirm_authorized=false, the server 400s 'confirm_authorized must be true', and the blank-remote target is POSTed too. The UI presented a ready no-confirm run that the server rejects. Filter blank targets and use one shared allDemo."
  },
  {
    "file": "scripts/compare-local.sh",
    "line": 125,
    "summary": "FM_ENTIRE_CLUSTER (documented 'EntireDB cluster host' override) only feeds the provisioning commands; the target remote POSTed to /api/runs comes from FM_ENTIRE_REMOTE (suggest default), so the two knobs are decoupled.",
    "failure_scenario": "A user sets FM_ENTIRE_CLUSTER=other.entire.io per the header docs. The repo is provisioned on other.entire.io, but the benchmark target remote stays the suggest-default cluster, so it pushes/clones against a cluster where the repo doesn't exist and the target dies not-found. FM_ENTIRE_REMOTE should default to https://$FM_ENTIRE_CLUSTER when the cluster is set."
  },
  {
    "file": "internal/server/runmgr.go",
    "line": 279,
    "summary": "secret_source credential CLIs (gh/glab/entire, up to 15s each) are exec'd and awaited (secWG.Wait) before the one-active-run check (m.active at line 291), so a POST that will be rejected with errRunActive still runs the operator's auth CLIs first.",
    "failure_scenario": "A run is active and a second start arrives (double-click Start, compare-local retry, two tabs). start() blocks up to 15s exec'ing credential helpers and materializing live tokens in memory, then discovers m.active != nil and returns 409. Do a cheap active-run pre-check before resolving secrets."
  },
  {
    "file": "cmd/forgemark/serve.go",
    "line": 21,
    "summary": "`forgemark serve -h` is treated as a hard error: ContinueOnError makes fs.Parse return flag.ErrHelp after printing usage, runServe propagates it, and main() prints 'forgemark: flag: help requested' and exits 1.",
    "failure_scenario": "A user runs `forgemark serve -h`, sees usage followed by a spurious error line and a non-zero exit, inconsistent with the classic CLI (which exits 0 on -h). Scripts checking exit status treat a help request as failure. Return nil when errors.Is(err, flag.ErrHelp)."
  },
  {
    "file": "internal/server/runmgr.go",
    "line": 238,
    "summary": "start() doesn't fast-validate real targets: empty repos, strategy=repo with <2 repos, and both secret and secret_source absent all pass POST validation and only fail later inside NewRunner in the coordinate() goroutine via markDead.",
    "failure_scenario": "An operator POSTs a target with no repos or no credential. Instead of an immediate 400 (as the CLI's parse/readSecret give), the server returns 200, creates a run, the target dies during setup, and if it was the only target the run silently transitions to state=failed; the cause is only in target_error events."
  },
